# Swan Compiler 2 — Control-flow analysis
#
# CFG.swan provides the executable, allocation-free graph verifier.
# Semantic control-flow analysis builds on verified CFGs to check:
# - definite initialization at every join,
# - all-path return completeness,
# - break/continue target legality,
# - reachability and unreachable statements,
# - path-sensitive ownership and borrow constraints.
#
# Current status: graph shape and reachability verification are implemented
# in CFG.swan and tested. AST-to-CFG construction, data-flow fixed points,
# definite initialization, return analysis, and ownership event generation
# remain unimplemented. Do not treat a structurally valid graph as proof that
# its source program is semantically valid.
